IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `qld-part06-amendment-and-repeal`

-- Tests for Part 6 (qld-part06-amendment-and-repeal.l4).
-- Each expected value was worked out by hand from the text, as cited.

§ `Tests of Part 6`

§§ `s 17A and s 19`

#ASSERT `an Act may be amended or repealed (s 17A)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `an Act may be amended or repealed (s 17A)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a provision of an Act is an Act in s 19 (s 19(1), definition Act)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a provision of an Act is an Act in s 19 (s 19(1), definition Act)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `expiry is a repeal in s 19 (s 19(1), definition repeal)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `expiry is a repeal in s 19 (s 19(1), definition repeal)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- SAYS If an Act is repealed by another Act, the first Act is not revived merely because the other Act is repealed (s 19(2)).
#ASSERT `the first Act is revived merely because the other Act is repealed (s 19(2))` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the first Act is revived merely because the other Act is repealed (s 19(2))` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the first Act is revived merely because the other Act is repealed (s 19(2))` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Examples 1 and 2 of s 19(2): Act A repeals Act B; Act A is repealed (by a later Act, or automatically under s 22C); Act B is not revived.
-- src:293 | Examples—
-- src:294 | 1 Act A repeals Act B. Act A is repealed. The repeal of Act A does not revive Act B.
-- src:295 | 2 Act A repeals Act B. Act A is automatically repealed under section 22C. The repeal of Act A does not revive Act B.
@ref s 19(2), examples 1 and 2 (src:293-295)
#ASSERT `the first Act is revived merely because the other Act is repealed (s 19(2))` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the first Act is revived merely because the other Act is repealed (s 19(2))` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- SAYS If an Act is amended by another Act, the amendments continue to operate, and the first Act is not revived in its form before the amendments, merely because the other Act is repealed (s 19(3)).
#ASSERT `the continuing operation of the amendments is affected merely because the other Act is repealed (s 19(3))` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the continuing operation of the amendments is affected merely because the other Act is repealed (s 19(3))` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the first Act is revived in the form it was in before the amendments took effect merely because of the repeal (s 19(3))` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the first Act is revived in the form it was in before the amendments took effect merely because of the repeal (s 19(3))` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Examples 1 and 2 of s 19(3): Act A amends Act B; Act A is repealed (later Act C, or automatically under s 22C); the amendments continue.
-- src:297 | Examples—
-- src:298 | 1 Act A amends Act B. Act A is repealed after it has commenced by a later Act C. The amendments made by Act A continue to operate, even though Act A has been repealed.
-- src:299 | 2 Act A amends Act B. Act A is automatically repealed under section 22C. The amendments made by Act A continue to operate, even though Act A has been repealed.
@ref s 19(3), examples 1 and 2 (src:297-299)
#ASSERT `the continuing operation of the amendments is affected merely because the other Act is repealed (s 19(3))` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the continuing operation of the amendments is affected merely because the other Act is repealed (s 19(3))` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 19 limits s 20, s 20A or any provision of the law by which the repeal is made (s 19(4))` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the later omission of the provision affects the continuing operation of the law (s 19A)` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the later omission of the provision affects the continuing operation of the law (s 19A)` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the later omission of the provision affects the continuing operation of the law (s 19A)` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 20`

#ASSERT `a provision of an Act is an Act in s 20 (s 20(1), definition Act)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `expiry is a repeal in s 20 (s 20(1), definition repeal)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `expiry is a repeal in s 20 (s 20(1), definition repeal)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- SAYS The repeal or amendment of an Act does not revive anything not in force or existing at the time, nor affect its previous operation, accrued rights, penalties, investigations, the proof of anything, savings, repeals or transitional effects (s 20(2), (4)).
#ASSERT `the repeal or amendment of an Act revives or affects the thing (s 20(2) and (4))` `anything not in force or existing at the time the repeal or amendment takes effect` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the repeal or amendment of an Act revives or affects the thing (s 20(2) and (4))` `the previous operation of the Act or anything suffered, done or begun under the Act` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the repeal or amendment of an Act revives or affects the thing (s 20(2) and (4))` `a right, privilege or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under the Act` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the repeal or amendment of an Act revives or affects the thing (s 20(2) and (4))` `a penalty incurred in relation to an offence arising under the Act` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the repeal or amendment of an Act revives or affects the thing (s 20(2) and (4))` `an investigation, proceeding or remedy in relation to a right, privilege, liability or penalty mentioned in s 20(2)(c) or (d)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the repeal or amendment of an Act revives or affects the thing (s 20(2) and (4))` `the proof of anything that has happened` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the repeal or amendment of an Act revives or affects the thing (s 20(2) and (4))` `any right, privilege or liability saved by the operation of the Act` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the repeal or amendment of an Act revives or affects the thing (s 20(2) and (4))` `any repeal or amendment made by the Act` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the repeal or amendment of an Act revives or affects the thing (s 20(2) and (4))` `any savings, transitional or validating effect of the Act` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the repeal or amendment of an Act revives or affects the thing (s 20(2) and (4))` `anything else` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the step may be taken as if the repeal or amendment had not happened (s 20(3))` `the investigation, proceeding or remedy is started` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the step may be taken as if the repeal or amendment had not happened (s 20(3))` `the investigation, proceeding or remedy is continued` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the step may be taken as if the repeal or amendment had not happened (s 20(3))` `the investigation, proceeding or remedy is completed` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the step may be taken as if the repeal or amendment had not happened (s 20(3))` `the right, privilege or liability is enforced` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the step may be taken as if the repeal or amendment had not happened (s 20(3))` `the penalty is imposed` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the step may be taken as if the repeal or amendment had not happened (s 20(3))` `the penalty is imposed` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the step may be taken as if the repeal or amendment had not happened (s 20(3))` `any other step` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 20 limits s 19, s 20A or any provision of the law by which the repeal or amendment is made (s 20(5))` EQUALS FALSE

§§ `s 20A`

#ASSERT `a provision of an Act is an Act in s 20A (s 20A(1), definition Act)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `expiry is a repeal in s 20A (s 20A(1), definition repeal)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- SAYS The "declaratory or validating effect" of an Act that declares a thing for a saving or transitional purpose, "validates" a thing, or declares a thing consequentially does not end merely because the Act is repealed (s 20A(2)).
#ASSERT `the declaratory or validating effect of the Act ends merely because of the repeal of the Act (s 20A(2))` `declares a thing for a saving or transitional purpose (whether or not the Act is expressed to be made for a purpose of that type)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the declaratory or validating effect of the Act ends merely because of the repeal of the Act (s 20A(2))` `validates a thing that may otherwise be invalid` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the declaratory or validating effect of the Act ends merely because of the repeal of the Act (s 20A(2))` `declares a thing for a purpose that is consequential on a declaration mentioned in paragraph (a) or a validation mentioned in paragraph (b) (whether or not the Act is expressed to be made for a purpose of that type)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the declaratory or validating effect of the Act ends merely because of the repeal of the Act (s 20A(2))` `none of these` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The five examples (a licence carried over to another law; an instrument declared to have been "validly made"; a matter declared "valid" that is not justiciable; an instrument declared "valid" that is taken to be amended)
-- each illustrate one limb: (a), (b), (c), (c).
-- src:329 | Example of paragraph (a)—
-- src:330 | a provision stating that an existing licence under a repealed law is taken to be a licence of a particular kind under another law and authorising the imposition of conditions under the other law
-- src:331 | Example of paragraph (b)—
-- src:332 | a provision declaring an instrument to have been validly made and acts done in reliance on the instrument to have been validly done
-- src:333 | Examples of paragraph (c)—
-- src:334 | 1 a provision stating that a matter that is declared valid is not justiciable
-- src:335 | 2 a provision stating that an instrument that is declared valid is taken to have been amended in a particular way
@ref s 20A(2), examples (src:329-335)
#ASSERT `the declaratory or validating effect of the Act ends merely because of the repeal of the Act (s 20A(2))` `declares a thing for a saving or transitional purpose (whether or not the Act is expressed to be made for a purpose of that type)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the declaratory or validating effect of the Act ends merely because of the repeal of the Act (s 20A(2))` `validates a thing that may otherwise be invalid` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the declaratory or validating effect of the Act ends merely because of the repeal of the Act (s 20A(2))` `declares a thing for a purpose that is consequential on a declaration mentioned in paragraph (a) or a validation mentioned in paragraph (b) (whether or not the Act is expressed to be made for a purpose of that type)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the effect of the law ends merely because of its repeal (s 20A(3))` `the declared law` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the effect of the law ends merely because of its repeal (s 20A(3))` `the savings law` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the effect of the law ends merely because of its repeal (s 20A(3))` `the savings law` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a declaration may be made for s 20A(3) about the Act (s 20A(4))` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a declaration may be made for s 20A(3) about the Act (s 20A(4))` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the declaration implies that, in the absence of a declaration, another Act is not a law to which s 20A applies (s 20A(5))` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the declaration implies that, in the absence of a declaration, another Act is not a law to which s 20A applies (s 20A(5))` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 20A limits s 19, s 20 or any provision of the law by which the repeal is made (s 20A(6))` EQUALS FALSE

§§ `ss 20B and 20C`

#ASSERT `s 20B applies (s 20B(1))` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20B applies (s 20B(1))` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 20B applies (s 20B(1))` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the appointment, delegation or other thing continues to have effect after the commencement as if it had been done under the amended provision (s 20B(2))` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the appointment, delegation or other thing continues to have effect after the commencement as if it had been done under the amended provision (s 20B(2))` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the change is an amendment in s 20B (s 20B(3), definition amend)` `an amendment in the ordinary sense` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the change is an amendment in s 20B (s 20B(3), definition amend)` `omission and re-enactment in the same law (with or without modification)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "but does not include omit and re-enact in another law"
#ASSERT `the change is an amendment in s 20B (s 20B(3), definition amend)` `omission and re-enactment in another law` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the change is an amendment in s 20B (s 20B(3), definition amend)` `any other change` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a provision of an Act is an Act in s 20C (s 20C(1), definition Act)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- SAYS An act or omission that an Act makes an offence is only an offence if committed after the Act commences (s 20C(2)).
#ASSERT `the act or omission is an offence under the Act (s 20C(2))` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the act or omission is an offence under the Act (s 20C(2))` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the act or omission is an offence under the Act (s 20C(2))` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the increase applies to the offence (s 20C(3))` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the increase applies to the offence (s 20C(3))` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the increase applies to the offence (s 20C(3))` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 21 and 22`

-- SAYS Repealed provisions that an Act replaces by new provisions continue in force until the new provisions commence (s 21).
#ASSERT `the repealed provisions continue in force (s 21)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the repealed provisions continue in force (s 21)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the repealed provisions continue in force (s 21)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `an Act and an Act amending it are to be read as one (s 22)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `an Act and an Act amending it are to be read as one (s 22)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 22A and 22B`

#ASSERT `where the thing is to be inserted (s 22A)` `a subsection` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the appropriate numerical or alphanumerical position`
#ASSERT `where the thing is to be inserted (s 22A)` `a paragraph` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the appropriate alphabetical position`
#ASSERT `where the thing is to be inserted (s 22A)` `a subparagraph` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the appropriate numerical or alphanumerical position`
#ASSERT `where the thing is to be inserted (s 22A)` `a sub-subparagraph` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the appropriate alphabetical position`
#ASSERT `where the thing is to be inserted (s 22A)` `a definition` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the appropriate alphabetical position, determined on a letter-by-letter basis`
#ASSERT `where the thing is to be inserted (s 22A)` `another provision` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the appropriate numerical or alphanumerical position`
#ASSERT `where the thing is to be inserted (s 22A)` `an example, note or penalty` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the end of the provision`
-- the Act specifies the position: s 22A does not answer
#ASSERT `where the thing is to be inserted (s 22A)` `a paragraph` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a subsection not to form part of a series: (1) does not apply
#ASSERT `where the thing is to be inserted (s 22A)` `a subsection` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `regard may be had to current Queensland legislative drafting practice (s 22A(8))` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `regard may be had to current Queensland legislative drafting practice (s 22A(8))` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the amendment is to be made at the place in the provision (s 22B)` `omitting a word` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the amendment is to be made at the place in the provision (s 22B)` `omitting a word and inserting another word` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the amendment is to be made at the place in the provision (s 22B)` `inserting a word before or after a particular word` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the amendment is to be made at the place in the provision (s 22B)` `omitting a word` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the amendment is to be made at the place in the provision (s 22B)` `any other amendment` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 22C`

#ASSERT `a repeal under s 22C(1) has effect for all purposes, including ss 19 to 20A (s 22C(2))` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a repeal under s 22C(1) has effect for all purposes, including ss 19 to 20A (s 22C(2))` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 22C limits the operation of any other provision of this Act about repeals (s 22C(3))` EQUALS FALSE
-- Example 1: a long title, a provision about citation, about commencement, amending and repealing provisions, and a provision about s 20A: an amending Act.
-- src:393 | Example 1—
-- src:394 | The Hypothetical Amending Act 1995 amends the ABC Act and the LMN Act. It also repeals a list of Acts set out in a schedule. Apart from—
-- src:395 | • a long title
-- src:396 | • a provision about the Act’s citation (that is, the Act’s short title)
-- src:397 | • a provision about the Act’s commencement
-- src:398 | • amending provisions (that is, provisions stating that the ABC Act and the LMN Act are amended and the provisions amending the Acts)
-- src:399 | • repealing provisions (that is, a provision stating that the Acts set out in the schedule are repealed and a schedule)
-- src:400 | • a provision about the application of section 20A to a provision being repealed;
-- src:401 | the Hypothetical Amending Act 1995 contains no other provisions. Its repealing provisions commence on assent, 21 March 1995. Its amending provisions commence on proclamation, 12 April 1995. Under subsection (1), the Hypothetical Amending Act 1995 is automatically repealed at the beginning of 13 April 1995.
@ref s 22C(4), example 1 (src:393-401)
#ASSERT `an Act is an amending Act (s 22C(4), definition amending Act)` (LIST `the Act's long title`, `a provision about the Act's citation`, `a provision about the Act's commencement`, `a provision providing for the amendment or repeal of an Act or other instrument (including a provision identifying the amended or repealed instrument)`, `a provision declaring an Act or a provision of an Act to be a law to which section 20A applies`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Example 2: the Act contains provisions establishing a new scheme, so it is not an amending Act.
-- src:402 | Example 2—
-- src:403 | The Example Act 1995 contains provisions establishing a new scheme. It also amends several Acts and repeals others. Because it contains the scheme provisions, it is not an amending Act covered by subsection (1).
@ref s 22C(4), example 2 (src:402-403)
#ASSERT `an Act is an amending Act (s 22C(4), definition amending Act)` (LIST `the Act's long title`, `any other provision`, `a provision providing for the amendment or repeal of an Act or other instrument (including a provision identifying the amended or repealed instrument)`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- SAYS An amending Act is an Act that consists only of the listed types of provision, so one extra provision of another type takes it outside the definition (s 22C(4)).
#ASSERT `an Act is an amending Act (s 22C(4), definition amending Act)` (LIST `the Act's preamble`, `a provision providing for the extension of the period before commencement, under section 15DA(2), of an Act or a provision of an Act that has not commenced within 1 year of the assent day`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the assent day in s 22C (s 22C(4), definition assent day)` TRUE (Date 5 4 1995) (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS Date 5 4 1995
#ASSERT `the assent day in s 22C (s 22C(4), definition assent day)` FALSE (Date 5 4 1995) (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS Date 1 1 2000
